    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.87) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.26). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Spencer Arrighetti; his 16% boost from the pitcher\u2019s skill rating combined with a leadoff spot makes him our most bankable asset. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** draws a ripe matchup against Randy Dobnak. With a high SP_xERA of 4.99 and a 13% dynamic platoon edge, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned to anchor the outfield production. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) also cleared the 70-point threshold, the trio of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67)\u2014who is thriving against the struggling Shane Bieber\u2014forms a formidable foundation for our offensive output.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just outside the starting lineup with a 58.79 score. While **Nasim Nunez** possesses the elite sprint speed we covet for the SB category, the optimizer ultimately favored the superior lineup positioning of our starters. His projected ninth-order slot carried a -8% penalty, which pushed him behind **Drake Baldwin** (58.04) and **Heliot Ramos** (44.19) once team-wide efficiency caps and positional scarcity were factored in. Caution is advised across the board as every rostered player is currently sitting on \"Lineup Pending\" status; specifically, **Kyle Tucker** (55.62) and **Andy Pages** (51.65) face a risk-heavy matchup against Ryan Weathers. Weathers\u2019 3.41 xERA significantly dampens the expected output for these two, and if the official lineups shift them lower in the order, their efficiency scores could drop below our preferred floor.",
